# memory_gap_shared_tables: Two tasks over one page table: task 2's task root names task 1's page-table root, so the two see the same guest pages at the same VAs (the host walks whatever table the root names). Task 2's object list is at VA page 2, task 1's at 0. Task 1 fills a buffer at VA 8; task 2, whose buffer record names the same VA page, copies it into its own buffer at VA 9: the copy shows the fill. Then task 2 fills the page and task 1 copies it. In the blocks setup each task maps the pages into its own host task; in the isolate setup each task has its own service, both over the one shared guest RAM.
